      "MADISON, Wis.  —  Ryan Hopkins, a quarterback prospect visiting Wisconsin, was over 2,000 miles from his home, yet he felt completely at home.",
       "“I felt the energy from the city,” said Hopkins, a former three-star recruit out of Mater Dei in Santa Ana, California. “I felt the energy from the coaches.",
        "But there was a hitch, aside from the distance. Hopkins had to cope with the dilemma that faces nearly every high school quarterback recruit, because most Bowl Subdivision institutions now rely heavily on transfers at that position: About 65% of the FBS starting quarterbacks to begin this season transferred at some time in their careers.",
         "“It’s a whole different deal,” said Trent Dilfer, who’s seen quarterback recruiting from almost every perspective.",
          "Dilfer, a former Fresno State quarterback and first-round draft pick, was the starting quarterback for the Baltimore Ravens' Super Bowl winning squad in the 2000 season. He was the coach of a high school power at Lipscomb Academy in Nashville, Tenn., a college head coach at UAB and now is back at Lipscomb.",
           "He remembers when a high school quarterback could learn on the job. Colleges don't have to wait that long anymore because so many quarterbacks with starting experience are available each year, thanks to the NCAA erasing the necessity of sitting out a year before the 2021-22 season.",
            "“That was a game-changer,” Dilfer said. “Because instead of recruiting the kid, now you’re recruiting a man.",
            "Hopkins committed to Wisconsin despite with the Badgers heading into a fourth consecutive season starting a transfer quarterback. Hopkins spent the summer vying with Louisville transfer Deuce Adams for the opportunity to back up Old Dominion transfer Colton Joseph, who earned the starting nod in the Badgers’ season-opening loss to No. 4 Notre Dame on Sunday nite.",
       "“I think with this coaching staff, no matter if you’re the 2 or the 3 or the 1, they’re coaching every guy the same,” Hopkins said.",
        "Transfer is the new normal.Most of the larger programs are transfer-heavy, leaving fewer spaces on the roster for high school players.",
         "“If you’re a quarterback in this day and age, you have to earn it and you have to say, ‘I’m OK with taking less when I’m first getting recruited, because I want to get more when I show how good I am,’” Washington coach Jedd Fisch said.",
          "They also need to recognize that the college they choose in high school may not be where they end up.",
           "According to aggregate rankings of recruiting sites compiled by 247Sports, more than 80% of the top 50 quarterbacks from the 2023 class have transferred. The amount of top-50 QBs from that class to have attended at least three institutions is nearly twice the number who remained at one school.",
            "“A kid that used to be able to go to a middle-of-the-road SEC or ACC school, they can probably go now to a Group of Five school and play,” said Buford (Ga.) High coach Bryant Appling. “Because two years from now when they want to transfer or move up, they'll have a leg up on the kid who just comes out of high school and they're not sure of.”",
            "Big ambiguity from the transfer portal All of that activity makes it difficult for high school quarterbacks who sign with colleges in December, right before the transfer portal window begins. Most commit to their college plans months before that December deadline, not knowing who they could be competing against once they’ve signed up.",
       "“You’re fishing in the dark, so to speak,” said Jason Negro, the coach at St. John Bosco in Bellflower, California, whose roster of former quarterbacks includes Illinois’ Katin Houser and 2018 first-round choice Josh Rosen. You can't control it. “You might look at a roster in November or December -- then in January it looks completely different.",
        "College coaches aren’t going to stop recruiting high school quarterbacks altogether because they’d rather build multiyear starters than have to rely on the portal every year. But the portal lets them be more selective.",
