            "Teddy Jarrard is now playing his senior season at Notre Dame instead of at North Cobb High School in Kennesaw, Georgia. Notre Dame has also received a verbal commitment from Champ Monds, who redshirted his junior season at Vero Beach High in Florida and will begin his college career next year. Julian Lewis of Colorado also moved up.",
             "There are some guys ready to do that,” Schiano said. “They’re grown enough. They’re adults. Other dudes. Not even close.”",
          "Experience counts The transfer gateway is bad news for high school quarterback prospects in the short term – but may pay off in the long run. Quarterbacks not heavily recruited out of high school can work their way up.",
           "If they just get in there and play, even at the I-AA level, you’ve seen people who have made great jumps come up.” Duke coach Manny Diaz said. “We’ve seen D-II guys that in the past would have been stuck there forever and nobody would have ever known about them.”",
            "Diego Pavia spent time at New Mexico Military Institute, New Mexico State and Vanderbilt and was the 2025 Heisman Trophy runner-up. Division II Ferris State alum Trinidad Chambliss began his career there, leading Mississippi to a College Football Playoff quarterfinal last year and is back behind center for the Rebels this season.",
